#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""rush00 — drop a team, get an evaluation sheet.

    rush00 serve [--port N]     the web visualizer (drop teams in the browser)
    rush00                      evaluate every team folder in rush00/repo
    rush00 <dir|git-url> ...    evaluate (and clone, for a URL) those teams
    rush00 subject <pdf|txt>    load the real subject of the day into subject.txt
    rush00 init                 write a blank subject.txt template

options:
    --leader LOGIN   team leader (picks the assigned rush if subject.txt has `assign`)
    --rush N         the assigned rush number, if you already know it
    --open           open the report in the browser when done
    --no-norm        skip norminette

The core of rush00 is fixed (rush(x, y) draws an x-wide, y-tall rectangle from
a 3x3 pattern of corner/edge/fill chars, x==1 keeps the left column, y==1
keeps the top row; files main.c ft_putchar.c rush0X.c; only write allowed).
What changes between subject versions (the chars, the examples, file names,
flags, the assignment rule) is read from subject.txt next to this script.
Without it every rush is checked for self-consistency against the team's own
output and its pattern is shown for you to compare with the PDF.
"""

